{"Utrecht":{"id":"6fdc26a2-ee6e-4609-bd52-b9e566a2fe6b","word":"Utrecht","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"city in the Netherlands","word":"Utreque"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"province of the Netherlands","word":"Utreque"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The Treaty of Utrecht (11 April 1713) recognized Anne as the rightful queen of England and yielded St Kitts and much of Canada to the English.","bold_text_offsets":[[14,21]],"type":"example","id":"0f0afce4-4e1e-4964-be02-a3407953fb13"}],"categories":["English terms with usage examples","en:Cities in Utrecht, Netherlands","en:Cities in the Netherlands","en:Municipalities of Utrecht, Netherlands","en:Places in Utrecht, Netherlands","en:Places in the Netherlands","en:Provincial capitals of the Netherlands"],"links":[["city","city"],["municipality","municipality"],["capital","capital"],["Utrecht","Utrecht#English"],["Netherlands","Netherlands#English"]],"glosses":["A city and municipality, the capital of Utrecht province, Netherlands."],"id":"3aee5379-5d57-4f13-86a4-ced0c1998c50"},{"examples":[{"text":"E.g. muug 'tired' in the Utrecht dialect (Ponelis 1990: 36). Utrechtian, which does not delete intervocalic [χ/ɣ], belongs to the group of Hollandic dialects, which is the Dutch dialect group most closely related to Afrikaans.","ref":"2012, Hans den Besten, edited by Ton van der Wouden, Roots of Afrikaans: Selected writings of Hans den Besten (series: Creole Language Library 44), John Benjamins Publishing Company: Amsterdam / Philadelphia, p. 81","id":"07e8d7d6-a1f5-4132-ba29-2c29818e3d3c"}],"categories":["en:Places in the Netherlands","en:Provinces of the Netherlands","en:Utrecht, Netherlands"],"links":[["province","province"],["Netherlands","Netherlands#English"]],"glosses":["A province of the Netherlands."],"id":"da76feea-5be3-4ce4-bea8-2c5206d2a82a"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"Utraquism":{"id":"4ddf0f71-7d71-47b1-ab66-00132